Z||000005||william_thorniii||05-25-2000||09:18 PM||||Welcome Mike!<P>I too am the proud owner of a 1987 EC with the 2.5L 4 banger.  When I first got it I spent over $1000 on her trying to get her to overcome the same symptoms that you describe.  After much $ and frustration, I began to notice a pattern.  The car would only act like this when the temp was cold and or there was high humidity in the air.  Then I also realized that after reaching operating temperature, the problems went away.  I hope this helps. <P>Also a tip... on the distributorless ignition, you cannot change your plug wires enough.  They really chew through (even the good sets) rather quickly and their electrical system is EXTREMELY picky. <P>William T. Thorn, III<BR>(Heading to HI on honeymoon in Sept.)||||reg||10
